#: ../../BaTiO3/introduction.rst:5
msgid "導入"
msgstr "Introduction"

#: ../../BaTiO3/introduction.rst:7
msgid ""
"BaTiO₃（チタン酸バリウム）は、温度によって結晶構造と分極の向きが変わります。\\ この連載では Quloud を使い、どの構造が 0 K "
"で最も安定か、昇温するとその構造がどう変わるかを調べます。"
msgstr ""
"The crystal structure and polarization direction of BaTiO₃ (barium "
"titanate) change with temperature. \\  In this series, we use Quloud to "
"investigate which structure is most stable at 0 K and how it changes upon"
" heating."

#: ../../BaTiO3/introduction.rst:11
msgid "温度と分極の向き"
msgstr "Temperature and Polarization Direction"

#: ../../BaTiO3/introduction.rst:13
msgid ""
"X線回折などで決まる結晶構造は、原子の位置を多数の単位胞と測定時間について平均したもので、**平均構造** と呼ばれます。\\ "
"原子は熱で絶えず揺れているので、ある瞬間の原子配置はこの平均構造からずれています。\\ BaTiO₃ の平均構造は、低温から順に "
"**菱面体晶（R）→ 斜方晶（O）→ 正方晶（T）→ 立方晶（C）** と変わります。\\ 分極の向きは、\\ `擬立方晶 <https"
"://technical-notes.quemix.com/solid/pseudocubic.html>`__\\ の軸で菱面体晶が "
":math:`\\langle 111\\rangle`、斜方晶が :math:`\\langle 110\\rangle`、正方晶が "
":math:`\\langle 100\\rangle` です。\\ 室温では通常、正方晶相にあります。\\ 約 393 K "
"のキュリー温度を超えると、平均構造は常誘電の立方晶となります。\\ 4 相の空間群と分極の向きは技術ノートの\\ `4つの相と分極の向き "
"<https://technical-notes.quemix.com/solid/ferroelectricity.html#batio3"
"-four-phases>`__\\ にまとめました。"
msgstr ""
"The crystal structure determined by methods such as X-ray diffraction is "
"an **average structure**, obtained by averaging atomic positions over "
"many unit cells and over the measurement time. \\  Thermal motion "
"continuously shifts the atoms, so their instantaneous arrangement differs"
" from this average structure. \\  As temperature increases, the average "
"structure of BaTiO₃ follows the sequence **rhombohedral (R) → "
"orthorhombic (O) → tetragonal (T) → cubic (C)**. \\  In terms of the \\  "
"`pseudocubic <https://technical-"
"notes.quemix.com/solid/pseudocubic.html>`__ \\  axes, the polarization "
"directions are :math:`\\langle 111\\rangle` for rhombohedral, "
":math:`\\langle 110\\rangle` for orthorhombic, and :math:`\\langle "
"100\\rangle` for tetragonal. \\  At room temperature, BaTiO₃ is usually "
"in the tetragonal phase. \\  Above the Curie temperature of about 393 K, "
"the average structure becomes cubic and paraelectric. \\  The Technical "
"Notes section on \\  `the four phases and their polarization directions "
"<https://technical-notes.quemix.com/solid/ferroelectricity.html#batio3"
"-four-phases>`__ \\  lists the space groups and polarization directions "
"of the four phases."

#: ../../BaTiO3/introduction.rst:21
msgid ""
"高温の立方晶相でも、瞬間的には Ti が酸素八面体の中心からずれることがあります（技術ノートの\\ `局所的なTiの変位と平均構造 <https"
"://technical-notes.quemix.com/solid/ferroelectricity.html#fe-local-"
"average>`__）。\\ 昇温計算では、局所変位と平均構造の両方を調べます。"
msgstr ""
"Even in the high-temperature cubic phase, Ti can momentarily move away "
"from the center of its oxygen octahedron (see the Technical Notes on \\  "
"`local Ti displacements and average structure <https://technical-"
"notes.quemix.com/solid/ferroelectricity.html#fe-local-average>`__). \\  "
"In the heating calculations, we examine both the local displacements and "
"the average structure."

#: ../../BaTiO3/introduction.rst:24
msgid ""
"BaTiO₃ は代表的なペロブスカイト型強誘電体で、誘電体、センサー、アクチュエーターなどに使われます。\\ 強誘電体は外部電場がなくても\\ "
"`自発分極 <https://technical-notes.quemix.com/solid/ferroelectricity.html"
"#spontaneous-polarization>`__\\ をもち、電場によってその向きを反転できます。\\ BaTiO₃ の分極には、Ti "
"と O が相対的にずれる\\ `極性ソフトモード <https://technical-"
"notes.quemix.com/solid/soft_mode.html#polar-soft-mode>`__、Ti–O 結合での\\ "
"`軌道の混成 <https://technical-"
"notes.quemix.com/solid/ferroelectric_origin.html#fo-"
"hybridization>`__、格子のひずみが関わります。"
msgstr ""
"BaTiO₃ is a representative perovskite ferroelectric, used in dielectrics,"
" sensors, and actuators, among other applications. \\  Ferroelectrics "
"exhibit \\  `spontaneous polarization <https://technical-"
"notes.quemix.com/solid/ferroelectricity.html#spontaneous-polarization>`__"
" \\  even without an external electric field, and an electric field can "
"reverse its direction. \\  Polarization in BaTiO₃ involves a \\  `polar "
"soft mode <https://technical-notes.quemix.com/solid/soft_mode.html#polar-"
"soft-mode>`__, in which Ti and O are displaced relative to one another, "
"\\  `orbital hybridization <https://technical-"
"notes.quemix.com/solid/ferroelectric_origin.html#fo-hybridization>`__ in "
"Ti–O bonding, and lattice strain."

#: ../../BaTiO3/introduction.rst:29
msgid "計算で調べること"
msgstr "What the Calculations Probe"

#: ../../BaTiO3/introduction.rst:31
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
":numref:`{number}. {name} <batio3-doc-lattice-constant>` と "
":numref:`{number}. {name} <batio3-doc-stability>` では、4 相の格子定数と 0 K "
"での相対エネルギーを求めます。\\ :numref:`{number}. {name} <batio3-doc-geometry-"
"optimization>` では、正方晶の格子を固定し、原子を緩和して Ti と O の相対変位を比較します。"
msgstr ""
"In :numref:`{number}. {name} <batio3-doc-lattice-constant>` and "
":numref:`{number}. {name} <batio3-doc-stability>`, we determine the "
"lattice constants and relative energies of the four phases at 0 K. \\  "
":numref:`{number}. {name} <batio3-doc-geometry-optimization>` describes "
"how we relax the atoms at a fixed tetragonal lattice and compare the "
"relative displacements of Ti and O."

#: ../../BaTiO3/introduction.rst:33
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
":numref:`{number}. {name} <batio3-doc-total-energy-dft-mlip>` と "
":numref:`{number}. {name} <batio3-doc-total-energy>` "
"では、原子をずらすとエネルギーがどれだけ下がるかを調べます。\\ Part 1 では Ti だけを動かし、Part 2 では Ba・Ti・O "
"の協同変位と格子ひずみ・体積の影響を調べます。"
msgstr ""
"In :numref:`{number}. {name} <batio3-doc-total-energy-dft-mlip>` and "
":numref:`{number}. {name} <batio3-doc-total-energy>`, we examine how much"
" the energy decreases when the atoms are displaced. \\  In Part 1, we "
"move only Ti. In Part 2, we examine the cooperative displacements of Ba, "
"Ti, and O and the effects of lattice strain and volume."

#: ../../BaTiO3/introduction.rst:35
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
":numref:`{number}. {name} <batio3-doc-phase-transition>` "
"では、分子動力学（MD）で温度を上げ、Ti の局所変位と格子定数から相の変化を追います。"
msgstr ""
"In :numref:`{number}. {name} <batio3-doc-phase-transition>`, we raise the"
" temperature in molecular dynamics (MD) simulations and track phase "
"changes using local displacements of Ti and lattice constants."

#: ../../BaTiO3/introduction.rst:37
msgid ""
"0 K の全エネルギーは各構造の相対安定性を比べる基準になります。\\ 有限温度でどの相が安定かを熱力学的に決めるには、温度ごとの\\ "
"`自由エネルギー <https://technical-"
"notes.quemix.com/thermo/gibbs_energy.html>`__\\ が必要になります。\\ "
"機械学習原子間ポテンシャル（MLIP）の結果は、学習データの適用範囲を踏まえ、密度汎関数理論（DFT）の結果との差を確認して解釈します。\\ "
"MLIP の仕組みと検証の観点は技術ノートの\\ `機械学習原子間ポテンシャル <https://technical-"
"notes.quemix.com/md/mlip.html>`__\\ で説明しています。"
msgstr ""
"Total energies at 0 K provide a basis for comparing the relative "
"stability of the structures. \\  Determining which phase is "
"thermodynamically stable at finite temperature requires the \\  `free "
"energy <https://technical-notes.quemix.com/thermo/gibbs_energy.html>`__ "
"\\  at each temperature. \\  We interpret the results from machine-"
"learning interatomic potentials (MLIPs) by taking into account the scope "
"of the training data and checking differences from density functional "
"theory (DFT) results. \\  The Technical Notes article on \\  `machine-"
"learning interatomic potentials <https://technical-"
"notes.quemix.com/md/mlip.html>`__ \\  explains how MLIPs work and what to"
" check when validating them."

